    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-8ma0-01-specimen/q4",
      "question": "<figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:87mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-8ma0-01-specimen/q04-figure.svg\" alt=\"Figure 1. Sketch of the curve y = g(x).\"></figure><p>Figure 1 shows a sketch of the curve with equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y = g(x)\"></span>.</p><p>The curve has a single turning point, a minimum, at the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"M(4, -1.5)\"></span>.</p><p>The curve crosses the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span>-axis at two points, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P(2, 0)\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"Q(7, 0)\"></span>.</p><p>The curve crosses the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\"></span>-axis at a single point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R(0, 5)\"></span>.</p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(a) State the coordinates of the turning point on the curve with equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y = 2g(x)\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(b) State the largest root of the equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"g(x + 1) = 0\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p><span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(c) State the range of values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span> for which <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"g&#x27;(x) \\leq 0\"></span></p><p><span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></p><p>Given that the equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"g(x) + k = 0\"></span>, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span> is a constant, has no real roots,</p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(d) state the range of possible values for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></p>",
