      "id": "exam/edexcel-8ma0-01-specimen/q5",
      "question": "<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(x) = x^3 + 3x^2 - 4x - 12\"></span></p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(a) Using the factor theorem, explain why <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(x)\"></span> is divisible by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(x + 3)\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(b) Hence fully factorise <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(x)\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(c) Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{x^3 + 3x^2 - 4x - 12}{x^3 + 5x^2 + 6x}\"></span> can be written in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A + \\frac{B}{x}\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\"></span> are integers to be found.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></p>",
