      "question": "<p class=\"exam-subpart\">(i) Use a counter example to show that the following statement is false.</p><p>“<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n^2 - n - 1\"></span> is a prime number, for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3 \\leq n \\leq 10\"></span>.”</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(ii) Prove that the following statement is always true.</p><p>“The difference between the cube and the square of an odd number is even.”</p><p>For example <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"5^3 - 5^2 = 100\"></span> is even.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></p>",
