    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-8ma0-01-specimen/q8",
      "question": "<figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:105mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-8ma0-01-specimen/q08-figure.svg\" alt=\"Figure 2. Area under the square-root graph.\"></figure><p>Figure 2 shows a sketch of the curve with equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y = \\sqrt{x}\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x \\geqslant 0\"></span></p><p>The region <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\"></span>, shown shaded in Figure 2, is bounded by the curve, the line with equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x = 1\"></span>, the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span>-axis and the line with equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x = a\"></span>, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span> is a constant.</p><p>Given that the area of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\"></span> is 10</p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(a) find, in simplest form, the value of</p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(i) <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\int_{1}^{a} \\sqrt{8x} \\, dx\"></span></p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(ii) <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\int_{0}^{a} \\sqrt{x} \\, dx\"></span></p><p><span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(b) show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a = 2^k\"></span>, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span> is a rational constant to be found.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></p>",
