    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-8ma0-01-specimen/q12",
      "question": "<figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:89mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-8ma0-01-specimen/q12-figure-1.svg\" alt=\"Figure 3. Line and curve intersecting at A.\"></figure><p>Figure 3 shows a sketch of the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> with equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y = 3x - 2\\sqrt{x}\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x \\geqslant 0\"></span> and the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l\"></span> with equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y = 8x - 16\"></span>.</p><p>The line cuts the curve at point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> as shown in Figure 3.</p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(a) Using algebra, find the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span> coordinate of point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></p><p>(b)</p><figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:85mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-8ma0-01-specimen/q12-figure-2.svg\" alt=\"Figure 4. Unshaded region R.\"></figure><p>The region <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\"></span> is shown unshaded in Figure 4. Identify the inequalities that define <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></p>",
      "steps": [
