      "id": "exam/edexcel-8ma0-01-specimen/q13",
      "question": "<p>The growth of pond weed on the surface of a pond is being investigated.</p><p>The surface area of the pond covered by the weed, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A \\text{ m}^2\"></span>, can be modelled by the equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"A = 0.2 \\text{e}^{0.3t}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\"></span> is the number of days after the start of the investigation.</p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(a) State the surface area of the pond covered by the weed at the start of the investigation.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(b) Find the rate of increase of the surface area of the pond covered by the weed, in <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\text{m}^2/\\text{day}\"></span>, exactly 5 days after the start of the investigation.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p><p>Given that the pond has a surface area of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"100 \\text{ m}^2\"></span>,</p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(c) find, to the nearest hour, the time taken, according to the model, for the surface of the pond to be fully covered by the weed.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></p><p>The pond is observed for one month and by the end of the month 90% of the surface area of the pond was covered by the weed.</p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(d) Evaluate the model in light of this information, giving a reason for your answer.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></p>",
